oons]] [[Cookbook:Lime|lime]] or [[Cookbook:Lemon|lemon]] juice\n* ½–1 teaspoon (2–4 g) [[Cookbook:Salt|salt]]\n* 100 ml (½ cup) ice cubes\n* ¼ teaspoon [[Cookbook:Mint|mint]] (finely crumbled, dried; optional)\n* 1 small [[Cookbook:Pinch|pinch]] of [[Cookbook:Cayenne pepper|cayenne pepper]] (optional)\n\n== Procedure ==\n# Dry-roast cumin seeds by cooking them over low heat in a small pan until you can smell the seasoning (about 2–3 minutes). Cool and grind.\n# In [[Cookbook:Blender|blender]], blend cumin seed powder with yoghurt, milk, lemon juice, salt, and ice cubes.\n# Serve chilled, optionally garnished with crumbled mint and a small pinch of cayenne.\n\n[[Category:Indian recipes]]\n[[Category:South Asian recipes]]\n[[Category:Recipes for lassi]]\n[[Category:Recipes using milk]]\n[[Category:Recipes using cumin]]\n[[Category:Recipes using lime juice]]\n[[Category:Recipes using lemon juice]]\n[[Category:Recipes using cayenne]]\n[[Category:Recipes using mint]]","isRecipe":true,"recipe":{"name":"Mild Salty Lassi","nameAr":null,"servings":null,"servingsSourceText":"4","ingredients":[{"id":"source-line-1","name":"1 teaspoon (4 g) cumin seeds","sourceText":"1 teaspoon (4 g) cumin seeds","amountText":"1 teaspoon (4 g) cumin seeds","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-2","name":"250 ml (1 cup) full-fat yogurt","sourceText":"250 ml (1 cup) full-fat yogurt","amountText":"250 ml (1 cup) full-fat yogurt","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-3","name":"250 ml (1 cup) chilled milk","sourceText":"250 ml (1 cup) chilled milk","amountText":"250 ml (1 cup) chilled milk","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-4","name":"2 teaspoons lime or lemon juice","sourceText":"2 teaspoons lime or lemon juice","amountText":"2 teaspoons lime or lemon juice","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-5","name":"½–1 teaspoon (2–4 g) salt","sourceText":"½–1 teaspoon (2–4 g) salt","amountText":